DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnmmttoossggii  reads  a PNM image as input and produces an SGI image file as
       output.  The SGI image will be 2-dimensional (1 channel)  for  PBM  and
       PGM input, and 3-dimensional (3 channels) for PPM.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppnnmmttoossggii  recognizes  the
       following command line options:



       --vveerrbbaattiimm
              Write an uncompressed file.

       --rrllee (default)
              Write a compressed (run length encoded) file.

       --iimmaaggeennaammee _n_a_m_e
              Write  the string "name" into the imagename field of the header.
              The name string is limited to 79  characters.   If  no  name  is
              given, pnmtosgi writes "no name" into this field.



